to flip on the live link.\\n\\n## 📤 Step 1 — Upload the file\\n1. Go to your **Rando** repo page on github.com (you'll be looking at it now — probably says *\\\"quick setup\\\"* or shows a mostly empty repo).\\n2. Click **Add file** (top right, near the green Code button) → **Upload files**.\\n3. Drag your **`Rant-o-Meter.html`** file into the box (or click *\\\"choose your files\\\"* and pick it).\\n4. Scroll down to **Commit changes** and click the green **Commit changes** button. That's it — the file's in. ✅\\n\\n## 🌐 Step 2 — Turn on GitHub Pages (this makes it clickable)\\n1. In your repo, click **Settings** (top menu of the repo).\\n2. Down the **left sidebar**, click **Pages**.\\n3. Under **\\\"Build and deployment\\\"** → **Source**, choose **Deploy from a branch**.\\n4. Under **Branch**, pick **main** (or *master*), leave the folder as **/ (root)**, and click **Save**.\\n5. Wait about **1–2 minutes**, then refresh that page. A green banner appears with your live link.\\n\\n## 🔗 Step 3 — Your shareable link\\nYour URL will look like this:\\n\\n```\\nhttps://YOUR-USERNAME.github.io/Rando/Rant-o-Meter.html\\n```\\n\\nJust swap in your actual GitHub username. Send *that* link to anyone — they click it and the meter loads live in their browser, buttons and all. 🖱️🔥\\n\\n## ⚡ Pro tip\\nIf you rename the file to **`index.html`** instead of `Rant-o-Meter.html`, the link gets shorter and cleaner:\\n\\n```\\nhttps://YOUR-USERNAME.github.io/Rando/\\n```\\n\\nBoth work — `index.html` just looks tidier when you share it.\\n\\n---\\n\\nGive Step 1 a crack and tell me what you see — if the **Pages** section looks different or the link throws a 404 (it sometimes needs a couple minutes to wake up), ping me and I'll sort it. What's your GitHub username, so I can give you the exact link to test? ☕\",\"turnState\":\"Completed\",\"author\":\"bot\",\"responseIdentifier\":\"Default\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-09-04T00:27:46.8536846+00:00\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-04T00:27:46.8536846+0